        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 53,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 21 shared diagram, upper left",
          "description": "Unshaded triangle QPS, right-angled at P, with perpendicular altitude PR to the horizontal baseline QS. All ordinary outlines and labels use black. Coordinates are schematic and enforce both right angles without asserting numerical measurements.",
          "mathematics": "Q, R and S are collinear in that order; PR is perpendicular to QS; PQ is perpendicular to PS; QR=a, RS=b, PR=h and angle PQS=theta.",
